    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**, 21 tests, 0 failures (including the new address-normalization checkpoints Cp01, Cp10, Cp11, Cp12).\n\n## What I did\n\nAddress normalization is now applied to every owner creation. The canonical form trims and collapses whitespace, upper-cases, and expands whole-word abbreviations (`ST`\u2192`STREET`, `RD`\u2192`ROAD`, `AVE`\u2192`AVENUE`).\n\n**New files**\n- `AddressNormalizer.java` \u2014 a small shared, idempotent utility holding the normalization rule (null/whitespace-only \u2192 `\"\"`).\n- `NormalizeOwnerAddress.java` \u2014 a pipeline step that mutates the validated body in place (mirroring `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`/`NormalizeOwnerEmail`), so `BuildOwner`/`SaveOwner` store the normalized address and `GET` returns it.\n\n**Changed**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted `normalizeAddress` between `normalizeEmail` and `checkUnique`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`, so it runs before the household checks.\n- `ValidateOwnerFields.java` \u2014 the `address` required-field check now runs against the *normalized* value, so an address blank after normalization is a 400.\n- `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique.java` and `AssignHousehold.java` \u2014 address comparison (duplicate detection) and the shared `householdId` derivation now route through `AddressNormalizer.normalize`, so `\"12 Main St\"` and `\"12 main street\"` collide and share the same household id. (Last-name comparison keeps its own case-folding rule.)\n\nJavadocs on the touched steps were updated to describe the normalized-address behaviour.",
